2,0 $ Pileus with relatively short ( < 1 mm) setae ; pleurocystidia thick-walled (up to 6 µm) , often with a capitate to subcapitate and yellowish crystalline deposited apex (usually ca. 2 µm thick-walled) $ X. pudens
2,0 $ Pileus with long (up to 3 mm long) setae ; pleurocystidia thin-walled (mostly < 1 µm thick) with an occasionally subcapitate apex rarely with crystalline deposits $ X. melanotricha
3,4 $ Basidia 4- spored; pleurocystidia fusiform , capitate to subcapitate ; Asia
3,5 $ Basidia 2 or 4- spored; pleurocystidia slender fusiform , usually with a non-capitate apex; Central and South America
4,0 $ Basidiospores subglobose to broadly ellipsoid (Q = 1. 05- 1. 20); pleurocystidia thin-walled (mostly <= 0. 5 µm thick) , usually with non-capitate apex without crystalline deposits; mostly in subtropical and tropical areas $ X. sinopudens
4,0 $ Basidiospores broadly ellipsoid to ellipsoid (Q = 1. 10- 1. 40) ; pleurocystidia thick-walled (mostly 1-3 µm thick) , often with a capitate to subcapitate apex covered with crystalline deposits; mostly in temperate and subtropical areas $ X. strigosa
5,0 $ Basidia 2- spored; basidiospores subglobose to subovoid; Central and northern South America $ X. hispida
5,0 $ Basidia 4- or a mixture of 2- and 4- spored; basidiospores subglobose or broadly ellipsoid to ellipsoid; Central and South America $ X. setulosa
